WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.107
Shivaar, lesson three:
pointer five, SQLite.

00:00:05.227 --> 00:00:09.284
The helper class, CREATE
TABLE, the four queries,

00:00:09.404 --> 00:00:14.873
and the Cursor into an ArrayList
that feeds your RecyclerView.

00:00:14.993 --> 00:00:17.946
Then a real app,
four real mistakes,

00:00:18.066 --> 00:00:24.231
and two TODO questions in the
style of your CA question four.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:30.215
Slide six of Architecting Android
Lists: the data pipeline.

00:00:30.335 --> 00:00:34.848
Rows come out of SQLite,
each row becomes one object,

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:39.289
the objects go into an ArrayList,
and the Adapter shows it.

00:00:39.409 --> 00:00:41.858
Today we build the left half.

00:00:42.992 --> 00:00:46.208
The study guide,
page seventy-five:

00:00:46.328 --> 00:00:53.482
the recommended approach is a Database Helper
class that extends SQLiteOpenHelper.

00:00:53.602 --> 00:00:56.939
Its job is to create
and change the tables.

00:00:57.059 --> 00:01:00.876
The study guide puts the
queries in a second class.

00:01:00.996 --> 00:01:04.884
Your CA test put them in
the helper, and so do we.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:08.794
Page seventy-six explains it.

00:01:08.914 --> 00:01:12.683
The database needs a
name ending in dot db,

00:01:12.803 --> 00:01:15.612
and a version number
that starts at one.

00:01:15.732 --> 00:01:19.285
onCreate runs the CREATE
TABLE the first time.

00:01:19.405 --> 00:01:24.833
If the version in the code is higher
than on the phone, onUpgrade runs.

00:01:24.953 --> 00:01:29.226
Dropping and recreating the
table loses the user's data.

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:33.895
Pages seventy-nine
to eighty: insert.

00:01:34.015 --> 00:01:38.288
A ContentValues object holds
column and value pairs,

00:01:38.408 --> 00:01:41.481
and database dot
insert adds the row.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:45.442
The guide treats a result
above zero as success.

00:01:45.562 --> 00:01:51.386
Your CA memo checks not equal
to minus one. Both work.

00:01:52.533 --> 00:01:56.134
Page one hundred and
sixteen: the Cursor loop.

00:01:56.254 --> 00:01:58.847
rawQuery returns a Cursor.

00:01:58.967 --> 00:02:02.568
Move to the first record,
loop until the end,

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:06.672
add each value to the ArrayList,
and move to the next.

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:10.681
Forgetting moveToNext leaves
you in an infinite loop.

00:02:11.825 --> 00:02:15.186
Mastering Dynamic
Lists, slide nine:

00:02:15.306 --> 00:02:17.899
delete from the database first,

00:02:18.019 --> 00:02:22.795
then update the Adapter's list,
then notifyDataSetChanged.

00:02:22.915 --> 00:02:27.140
Page one hundred and twenty-
nine: delete takes the table,

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:30.069
a WHERE clause,
and its arguments.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.113
Slide twelve: if you
only query in onCreate,

00:02:35.233 --> 00:02:37.106
the list goes stale,

00:02:37.226 --> 00:02:40.154
because Back doesn't
run onCreate again.

00:02:40.274 --> 00:02:44.355
Query in onResume, and the
list is fresh every time.

00:02:45.492 --> 00:02:47.358
Whiteboard.

00:02:47.808 --> 00:02:52.153
PantryDbHelper extends
SQLiteOpenHelper.

00:02:52.603 --> 00:02:59.571
A database file name, ending in
dot db, and the version, one.

00:03:00.021 --> 00:03:07.241
The table name, and a constant per
column: underscore id, name, quantity.

00:03:07.691 --> 00:03:12.252
The CREATE TABLE goes in a
String, as on page seventy-six.

00:03:12.702 --> 00:03:16.831
The id is INTEGER PRIMARY
KEY AUTOINCREMENT,

00:03:17.281 --> 00:03:20.161
so SQLite numbers the rows.

00:03:20.611 --> 00:03:24.908
Name is TEXT NOT NULL,
quantity INTEGER NOT NULL.

00:03:25.358 --> 00:03:28.407
Watch the commas and
the closing bracket.

00:03:28.857 --> 00:03:32.050
The constructor passes
the name, null,

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.493
and the version to super.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:40.463
onCreate runs once, the first
time the database is used.

00:03:40.913 --> 00:03:44.874
It calls execSQL with
our CREATE TABLE.

00:03:45.324 --> 00:03:49.212
onUpgrade runs when the version
in the code is higher than

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.531
the one on the phone.

00:03:51.981 --> 00:03:58.495
The study guide's simple way: DROP
TABLE IF EXISTS, then onCreate.

00:03:58.945 --> 00:04:00.814
The rows are lost.

00:04:01.264 --> 00:04:03.425
ALTER TABLE would keep them.

00:04:04.908 --> 00:04:07.261
Create: the INSERT.

00:04:07.711 --> 00:04:11.600
getWritableDatabase,
because we change data.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:16.467
ContentValues holds the
pairs: name, and quantity.

00:04:16.917 --> 00:04:20.181
No id: SQLite fills it in.

00:04:20.631 --> 00:04:25.288
db dot insert returns the
new row id, or minus one.

00:04:25.738 --> 00:04:28.979
Return result not
equal to minus one.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.539
Read: the SELECT.

00:04:32.989 --> 00:04:36.302
An empty list, and a
readable database.

00:04:36.752 --> 00:04:41.192
rawQuery, SELECT star FROM
pantry, ordered by name.

00:04:41.642 --> 00:04:45.051
Null, because there's no
question mark to fill.

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:49.822
The cursor starts before the
first row, so moveToFirst.

00:04:50.272 --> 00:04:53.153
Then loop while it's
not after the last.

00:04:53.603 --> 00:04:58.428
Columns come in CREATE TABLE
order: getInt zero is the id,

00:04:58.878 --> 00:05:02.502
getString one the name,
getInt two the quantity.

00:05:02.952 --> 00:05:07.009
Build a PantryItem, add
it, then moveToNext.

00:05:07.459 --> 00:05:10.508
Forget it, and the
loop never ends.

00:05:10.958 --> 00:05:14.103
Close the cursor,
and return the list.

00:05:15.575 --> 00:05:19.632
Update: ContentValues with
only the new quantity.

00:05:20.082 --> 00:05:24.907
db dot update: the table, the
values, the WHERE clause,

00:05:25.357 --> 00:05:28.621
underscore id equals
question mark,

00:05:29.071 --> 00:05:32.000
and an array that fills
the question mark.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:35.307
It returns how
many rows changed.

00:05:35.757 --> 00:05:39.766
Delete is shorter: the table,
the same WHERE clause,

00:05:40.216 --> 00:05:42.086
and its argument.

00:05:42.536 --> 00:05:46.713
The question mark keeps you
safe from SQL injection.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.705
In the Activity, onCreate
makes the helper.

00:05:52.155 --> 00:05:56.908
onResume calls loadItems, so
the list is fresh every time.

00:05:57.358 --> 00:05:59.236
That's slide twelve.

00:05:59.686 --> 00:06:04.127
loadItems reads every row and
hands the list to the adapter,

00:06:04.577 --> 00:06:07.817
which calls notif
yDataSetChanged.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:12.708
The plus one button runs the
UPDATE, then loadItems again.

00:06:13.158 --> 00:06:15.751
Add and Delete
work the same way.

00:06:17.242 --> 00:06:21.106
The right half of the pipeline:
Lesson one's Adapter.

00:06:21.556 --> 00:06:26.237
It holds an ArrayList of
PantryItem, read from SQLite.

00:06:26.687 --> 00:06:30.720
setItems swaps in the fresh
list from the database,

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:34.411
then calls notifyDataSetChanged,

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:37.526
so the RecyclerView redraws.

00:06:37.976 --> 00:06:40.928
onBindViewHolder
casts the holder,

00:06:41.378 --> 00:06:45.939
gets one database row by
position, and sets its text:

00:06:46.389 --> 00:06:49.030
a String, never a bare int.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:52.721
getItemCount returns
the list's size:

00:06:53.171 --> 00:06:56.220
one screen row per database row.

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.221
This is the real project file.

00:07:00.341 --> 00:07:02.526
Every line has a comment,

00:07:02.646 --> 00:07:05.718
so you can revise from
it on your laptop.

00:07:06.867 --> 00:07:11.139
Gradle builds it, and adb
installs it on the emulator.

00:07:12.283 --> 00:07:16.196
On the emulator: I add
rice, eggs and milk.

00:07:16.316 --> 00:07:19.797
Each Add is an INSERT,
then a fresh SELECT.

00:07:19.917 --> 00:07:23.614
On the left is the real
database file afterwards,

00:07:23.734 --> 00:07:26.854
read on the phone with sqlite3.

00:07:26.974 --> 00:07:30.215
That's our CREATE
TABLE, word for word.

00:07:30.335 --> 00:07:34.320
Plus one on rice is an
UPDATE, so rice has three.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:38.041
Delete on milk is a
DELETE, so milk is gone.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:43.017
Mistake one: a missing
comma in CREATE TABLE.

00:07:43.137 --> 00:07:47.362
Java compiles it, because
to Java it's just a String.

00:07:47.482 --> 00:07:54.392
The first query crashes: SQLiteException, near
quantity, syntax error.

00:07:55.533 --> 00:07:57.397
Put the comma back.

00:07:57.517 --> 00:08:00.949
Reinstall, and onCreate
builds the table.

00:08:02.075 --> 00:08:06.276
Mistake two: I add a unit
column to CREATE TABLE,

00:08:06.396 --> 00:08:08.701
but leave the version at one,

00:08:08.821 --> 00:08:11.701
and install over
the old database.

00:08:11.821 --> 00:08:14.174
onCreate doesn't run again,

00:08:14.294 --> 00:08:17.319
so the old table
has no unit column.

00:08:17.439 --> 00:08:22.048
Insert fails: table pantry
has no column named unit.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.577
The fix: version two.

00:08:25.697 --> 00:08:30.258
Logcat shows onUpgrade,
one to two, then onCreate.

00:08:30.378 --> 00:08:32.256
Flour is saved.

00:08:32.376 --> 00:08:36.145
But rice is gone: drop
and recreate lost it,

00:08:36.265 --> 00:08:39.218
exactly as the
study guide warns.

00:08:40.367 --> 00:08:43.367
Mistake three: no moveToFirst.

00:08:43.487 --> 00:08:50.497
The cursor is still before the first row. Crash:
CursorIndexOutOfBoundsException,

00:08:50.617 --> 00:08:54.578
index minus one requested,
with a size of two.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.957
Put moveToFirst back.

00:08:58.077 --> 00:08:59.944
Both rows show.

00:09:01.075 --> 00:09:05.684
Mistake four: after the
INSERT, I forget loadItems.

00:09:05.804 --> 00:09:08.757
The screen still says zero rows.

00:09:08.877 --> 00:09:11.277
But the database has rice.

00:09:11.397 --> 00:09:14.662
The data is saved;
the list is stale.

00:09:15.783 --> 00:09:17.920
Put loadItems back.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:21.737
Rice shows, and eggs appears
the moment I add it.

00:09:22.867 --> 00:09:24.731
Key takeaways.

00:09:24.851 --> 00:09:26.724
Pause and copy them.

00:09:26.844 --> 00:09:30.253
Helper extends SQLiteOpenHelper.

00:09:30.373 --> 00:09:34.981
CREATE TABLE in onCreate, drop
and recreate in onUpgrade,

00:09:35.101 --> 00:09:36.971
and raise the version.

00:09:37.091 --> 00:09:39.732
ContentValues and insert.

00:09:39.852 --> 00:09:44.148
moveToFirst, loop,
moveToNext, close.

00:09:44.268 --> 00:09:47.269
Update and delete
with a question mark.

00:09:47.389 --> 00:09:50.582
And after every
change, query again.

00:09:51.742 --> 00:09:53.609
Your turn.

00:09:53.729 --> 00:09:57.690
Question one, in the style
of CA question four:

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:03.209
complete Smart Pantry's shopping
list helper. Four TODOs.

00:10:03.329 --> 00:10:06.234
Pause the video and
write it on paper.

00:10:27.367 --> 00:10:31.831
Question two: write update and
delete with a question mark,

00:10:31.951 --> 00:10:34.040
then keep the list fresh.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.071
Answer one.

00:10:57.191 --> 00:11:01.224
TODO one: execSQL
with CREATE TABLE:

00:11:01.344 --> 00:11:06.721
id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY
AUTOINCREMENT, item TEXT NOT NULL,

00:11:06.841 --> 00:11:09.169
amount INTEGER NOT NULL.

00:11:09.289 --> 00:11:13.634
TODO two: DROP TABLE IF
EXISTS, then onCreate.

00:11:13.754 --> 00:11:19.203
TODO three: ContentValues,
put item and amount, insert,

00:11:19.323 --> 00:11:22.732
and return result not
equal to minus one.

00:11:22.852 --> 00:11:27.365
TODO four: moveToFirst, loop
while not after the last,

00:11:27.485 --> 00:11:31.685
add a new ShoppingItem,
moveToNext, then close.

00:11:32.825 --> 00:11:34.695
Answer two.

00:11:34.815 --> 00:11:38.224
Update: ContentValues
with the amount,

00:11:38.344 --> 00:11:42.641
then db dot update with
id equals question mark,

00:11:42.761 --> 00:11:45.665
and the id as a
String in the array.

00:11:45.785 --> 00:11:49.290
Delete: the table, the
same WHERE clause,

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.279
and the same array.

00:11:51.399 --> 00:11:54.400
TODO three and four: loadItems,

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:57.328
after the delete
and in onResume.

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:02.699
Both answers, in a real
project: add milk and bread,

00:12:02.819 --> 00:12:05.628
plus one on milk, delete bread.

00:12:05.748 --> 00:12:11.698
The real database has the table,
and milk with three. Mark yourself.

00:12:12.825 --> 00:12:14.794
That's SQLite.

00:12:14.914 --> 00:12:19.019
Open the project, run it,
and break it on purpose.

00:12:19.139 --> 00:12:23.075
Send me photos of your two
answers, and I'll mark them.

00:12:23.195 --> 00:12:26.172
Next: XML layouts.

00:12:26.292 --> 00:12:28.477
You've got this, Shivaar.
